ence and expand structurally different compositions/edge cases before stronger generalization claims.","severity":"low","source_receipt_id":"expert-RMM-001-extended-pilot-v3-p0000-rotation0-forward-e95c3fe87aa2","source_role":"expert"},{"category":"lineage_discipline","evidence":"Cyclic variants share an underlying family. Request rotations can change write chronology; query rotations change output positions/IDs while preserving the per-query resolution rule. These are matched variants, not new independent semantic parents.","fix":"Keep all rotations and renderers in the same split and aggregate outcomes by the underlying family.","severity":"low","source_receipt_id":"expert-RMM-001-extended-pilot-v3-p0000-rotation0-forward-e95c3fe87aa2","source_role":"expert"}],"reason":"Both final independent reviewers ACCEPT this exact corrected record; target and hash binding pass independent-oracle evidence and adjudicator typed reexecution. Every semantic request/query within its source family now occupies every ID and position once across rotations; outcome classes cross those nuisance features, removing the prior deterministic ID/position shortcut. Variants remain one source parent/family/split. Remaining narrow fixtures, modest diversity and finite proxy limitations stay attached and restrict generalization claims.","receipt_id":"adj-extended-pilot-v3-b0666c6e569cb11f787d","record_hash":"e95c3fe87aa2a86d87c05659a0330cfefb2da4a5a093e8db1bcc133db0c2cba7","review_method":"Actual independent final adjudication of distinct-execution final receipts, typed target recheck and per-family nuisance/outcome crossing.","reviewer_execution_id":"/root/research_architect","reviewer_role":"independent_adjudicator","sample_id":"RMM-001-extended-pilot-v3-p0000-rotation0-forward","scope_limitations":["24 underlying independent families;196 renderings do not represent196 independent parents.","Same underlying model family carries correlated-error risk.","Explicit routing/protection is not empirical competence/retention; versioned retrieval is not learned persistent memory.","Earlier v2 REVISE receipts and disagreements remain historical evidence; new acceptance applies only to corrected exact hashes."],"scores":{"difficulty_quality":4,"diversity":2,"generalization_value":3,"instruction_clarity":5,"reasoning_validity":5,"semantic_correctness":5,"shortcut_resistance":3,"target_correctness":5}}
